  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14180691/assets/e5180db140f9567f6863eac3a4bedc498830c2f3e427d04480f61dfa3a64b3ce.png)\n\nLet $X$ be a random variable with the probability density function shown above. What are the modes of $X?$",
  "worked_solution": "The modes of a random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ are the values of $x$ at the global maxima of $f(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we can tell that the global maxima of $f(x)$ are at $x=4,7,10.$\n\nTherefore, the modes of $X$ are $4,7$ and $10.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14180691/assets/13de2513361cca92312190fb75d3c42a508de46efdc753ee6f6257c72e23c3e6.png)",
